                    insight_renew:          `The 31 sponsored seats (€4.05M) renew. You lifted ESG to a credible level, integrated and assessed it inside the core, balanced three residencies into one journey, and held the NPS floor — all inside 480 hours. That is integration, not addition.`,
                    insight_atrisk:         `Renewal is at risk. One or more of ESG coverage, integration quality, global balance or the +40 NPS floor fell short inside the cap — the sponsors will read this as a programme that met the letter and missed the point.`,
                    insight_boltedon:       `Integration quality stayed low: ESG reads as a bolt-on, not embedded in finance, strategy and operations. Sponsors will recognise the same “ESG felt bolted on” problem the redesign was meant to fix.`,
                    insight_npsbreach:      `Participant NPS fell through the +40 contractual floor. You solved for the sponsor and broke the participant — cutting the 4.6/5 core too hard costs you the satisfaction the contract also protects.`,
                    insight_unbalanced:     `Global balance is weak — the three residencies still feel like three trips. Either the hour split tilted toward one region or no connective thread binds the cities into one programme.`,
                    insight_overcap:        `You broke the 480-hour ceiling. Working executives, accreditation and employers all hold the line at 480 — a design that exceeds it is accumulation, not design, and is not deliverable.`,
                    insight_exemplar:       `Exemplary global design: ESG integrated and assessed, three residencies woven into one coherent leadership journey, the core protected and the sponsors renewed — the textbook answer to integration over addition under a hard constraint.`,
                    grade_atrisk:           `Renewal at Risk`,
